<title>USA: Witco completes sale of Golden Bear unit.</title>
<headline>Witco completes sale of Golden Bear unit.</headline>
<dateline>GREENWICH, Conn 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Witco Corp said Monday it had sold the assets of its Golden Bear Division to Golden Bear Acquisition Corp, a company formed by Glencoe Investment Corp of Chicago.</p>
<p>The sale was for about $50 million. Witco said it will use the proceeds to pay down debt.</p>
<p>The company is concentrating on its core competencies and the sale represents the final piece of its lubricants group.</p>
<p>Witco is a global chemical company providing high value specialty products. Its 1996 sales were $2.3 billion.</p>
</text>
